<div type="translation" resp="part:emfr">
      		
	<p n="1">The Fortune-bearer.</p>
	<p n="1">He whose quiver is wonderful.</p>
	
</div>
      	
      	
<div type="commentary">
         	
	<p>
		<ptr target="bib:Mahalingam1988_01"/> (IP 318)  translates as “The bearer of prosperity” and “The wonderful archer.” </p>
	<p>These appear to be <foreign>biruda</foreign>s of Narasiṁhavarman II Pallava, also attested in <ref target="DHARMA_INSPallava00054.xml">Pallava 54</ref>, <ref target="DHARMA_INSPallava00060.xml">Pallava 60</ref>, and <ref target="DHARMA_INSPallava00063.xml">Pallava 63</ref>.</p>
</div>
         	
